From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t3code-customize <t3code-customize@localhost>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 16:03:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] feat(server): compact idle threads before the prompt
 cache expires

Port of upstream PR pingdotgg/t3code#19662 (head 84698a79b865) onto the
installed nightly and the fork's patches. Opt-in setting "Compact idle
threads" (default off): an idle root thread compacts once in the last 10%
of its provider's prompt cache TTL, hidden from chat state, settlement,
pushes, sends, forks and limits.

Fork deviation: the context floor is 100k tokens
(MIN_IDLE_COMPACTION_CONTEXT_TOKENS), the floor Claude Code uses for its
own idle compaction, instead of the PR's 20k.

Fork interaction: the relay's idle-run filter also gates direct APNs push
(patches-tt/0004), and a child thread compacting while idle still settles
with its opener (patches-tt/0003).
